course: dictionary
lesson: 4572
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around the word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The helicopter landed on the hospital roof.» Landed and roof are clues that it is a flying machine.
explain: Sometimes a word is used in a special way. «Mum says Dad is a helicopter parent, always checking where I am.» Here helicopter is not an aircraft. It is an informal name for a parent who watches over a child too closely. Ask yourself: does the real meaning fit the sentence?
explain: To check, swap your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one. If it sounds silly, try another meaning from the dictionary.
fact: A helicopter is an aircraft with big spinning blades on top.
fact: A helicopter can go straight up, straight down and hover, which means stay still in one place in the air.
fact: «Helicopter» can also be a verb, meaning to carry someone by helicopter, but this is rare.
fact: «Helicopter parent» is an informal phrase for a parent who watches over a child too closely.
fact: Igor Sikorsky, born in Kyiv in 1889, built the first practical mass-produced helicopters, the VS-300 and R-4, in the USA.
exercise: «A rescue helicopter lifted the boy off the cliff.» What is a helicopter here? | *An aircraft with big spinning blades on top | A kind of bus for children | A bird that sings loudly | A boat with sails
exercise: Mum says, «Stop being a helicopter parent and let me walk to school alone.» What does helicopter parent mean? | A parent who likes helicopters | A parent who works on a farm | A parent who flies to school | *A parent who watches over a child too closely
exercise: «Sycamore seeds spin down like helicopters, so the wind can carry them away.» What does «like helicopters» tell you? | The seeds are real helicopters | The seeds can fly to the moon | *It is a comparison: the seeds move like helicopter blades | The seeds are made of metal
test: «The air ambulance landed on the hospital helicopter pad.» What is a helicopter pad? | A pad of paper for drawing | A cushion on a chair | *A flat place where helicopters land | A small pond in a garden
test: «Igor Sikorsky built the first practical mass-produced helicopters in the USA.» Where were they built? | *In the USA | On a farm in France | In Wales, near the cliffs | In Kyiv, where he was born
exam: «The helicopter hovered above the storm.» What does hovered mean here? | *Stayed still in one place in the air | Crashed into the sea | Spun very fast on the ground | Carried a parcel to the shop
